Subject: [PATCH] WhatsApp voice calls through meowcaller; session database in
 WAL mode

The call layer of reffehcsoibaf/neonize's call-enabled test build
(released 2026-10-24), as last updated on 2026-10-25: calls.go drives meowcaller
(github.com/purpshell/meowcaller, MIT) over the same whatsmeow client, with
no protobuf and no callbacks (CallsConfigure, CallsNextEvent, CallDial,
CallAnswer, CallHangup, CallReadAudio, CallWriteAudio). Neonize() installs
it per client and Stop() removes it.

The session database waits up to 30 s for a lock and uses WAL: under many
writes at once whatsmeow otherwise fails with "database is locked", and
calls and messages are lost.

go.mod points whatsmeow and meowcaller at the patched copies that
build_neonize.py prepares next to this checkout.
